gengtype: rename yybegin, which flex 2.6.5 and later define as a macro

Every C scanner that flex 2.6.5 or later generates defines a function-like
macro

    #define yybegin(s) (yy_start) = 1 + 2 * (s)

(src/cpp-flex.skl in flex; flex 2.6.4 defined only BEGIN). gengtype has its
own function of that name, declared in gengtype.h and defined in
gengtype-lex.l. The macro rewrites both, and the generated gengtype-lex.cc
no longer compiles:

    gengtype-lex.cc: error: variable or field 'yy_start' declared void
    gengtype.h: error: expected ')' before 'const'

Rename gengtype's function to gengtype_yybegin. parse_file in
gengtype-parse.cc is its only caller. The scanner's rules use BEGIN, which
flex still defines, so nothing else needs to change.

Not from upstream: GCC trunk still names the function yybegin (commit
d959aaea96ec, 2026-11-13).

